WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.414 --> 00:00:10.109
Diego Alvarez: Morning Marisol, morning Hector. How are things in Austin?

2
00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:21.610
Marisol Vega: Morning Diego. Things are good, busy. We're heading into what is usually our busiest stretch for residential solar in Texas, so we're getting the team ready.

3
00:00:22.231 --> 00:00:31.573
Hector Ruiz: Yeah, and the Spanish side is already seeing more calls, especially from the Meta campaigns. It's good, but we want to make sure we're staffed right.

4
00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:42.929
Diego Alvarez: That makes sense. September and October have been heavy for you the last couple of years. Do you have a sense of how much call volume you're expecting?

5
00:00:43.167 --> 00:00:56.051
Marisol Vega: We're planning for about a 30 percent increase over the summer baseline. Last year we hit around 4,200 calls a month in that window, and this year we're hoping to be closer to 5,500.

6
00:00:56.641 --> 00:01:02.707
Diego Alvarez: Okay, so a meaningful jump. Are you adding seats on the Invoca side for that?

7
00:01:03.635 --> 00:01:11.422
Marisol Vega: We are. We're bringing on eight new sales reps, mostly on the Spanish team, and two more on the English side.

8
00:01:11.422 --> 00:01:14.017
Marisol Vega: So that's ten new users to provision.

9
00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:22.636
Hector Ruiz: And a couple of them are starting next Monday, so we'd like them to have access before then if possible.

10
00:01:23.542 --> 00:01:31.499
Diego Alvarez: Let me pull up your user list. I can get the provisioning request started today. Do you have the names and emails ready?

11
00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:37.423
Marisol Vega: Hector has the list. He can send it over after this call.

12
00:01:38.078 --> 00:01:47.220
Hector Ruiz: Yes, I'll send it this afternoon. I have all ten with their emails. I'll also note which team they're on so the permissions are right.

13
00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:58.075
Diego Alvarez: Perfect. Once I have that, I'll submit the request and we should have them set up within two business days. That gets you ahead of Monday.

14
00:01:59.382 --> 00:02:10.049
Marisol Vega: Good. And speaking of training, we'd like to do a refresher for the whole team before the rush really hits. Is there a date that works on your side?

15
00:02:11.369 --> 00:02:18.207
Diego Alvarez: Let me check the calendar. I have the week of September 28 open. Would a Tuesday or Wednesday work?

16
00:02:18.954 --> 00:02:24.903
Hector Ruiz: Wednesday the 30th would be better. Tuesdays we have our pipeline review in the morning.

17
00:02:26.083 --> 00:02:28.516
Diego Alvarez: Okay, Wednesday the 30th. What time?

18
00:02:29.804 --> 00:02:36.128
Marisol Vega: Could we do 10 AM Central? That gives the West Coast folks time to get in.

19
00:02:36.888 --> 00:02:47.132
Diego Alvarez: 10 AM Central works. I'll send an invite and we can do a 45 minute session, with maybe 15 minutes for questions at the end.

20
00:02:48.278 --> 00:02:58.461
Hector Ruiz: That sounds good. Can we make sure the Spanish team gets a separate session too? Sometimes the examples in English don't land the same way.

21
00:02:59.704 --> 00:03:06.574
Diego Alvarez: Of course. We can do a second session in Spanish, maybe the following day, Thursday the 1st. Same time?

22
00:03:07.436 --> 00:03:12.575
Hector Ruiz: Thursday the 1st at 10, that works. I'll let the team know.

23
00:03:13.566 --> 00:03:21.859
Marisol Vega: And Diego, one more logistics thing. We're going to be running some new Google Ads campaigns in Arizona and Florida starting mid-October.

24
00:03:21.859 --> 00:03:26.383
Marisol Vega: We want to make sure the tracking numbers are set up correctly.

25
00:03:27.798 --> 00:03:33.573
Diego Alvarez: Got it. Do you have the campaign details yet, or is that still in progress?

26
00:03:34.943 --> 00:03:42.209
Marisol Vega: Still in progress. Our media team is finalizing the creative, but we expect to have the campaigns live by October 15.

27
00:03:42.209 --> 00:03:45.669
Marisol Vega: We'll need new tracking numbers for each campaign and state.

28
00:03:46.443 --> 00:04:00.634
Diego Alvarez: Okay, so roughly two weeks out. I can help coordinate with our provisioning team once you have the final list. Just send me the campaign names and the states, and we'll get the numbers set up.

29
00:04:02.115 --> 00:04:07.722
Hector Ruiz: Will those numbers also flow into Salesforce the same way? We rely on that for follow-up.

30
00:04:08.937 --> 00:04:19.900
Diego Alvarez: They should, as long as the campaigns are mapped correctly. We'll confirm that when we set them up. I'll make a note to check the Salesforce integration settings with you.

31
00:04:20.544 --> 00:04:35.344
Marisol Vega: Great. And one last thing, we're planning a team offsite in early November, just a half day. Would you be able to join us for a quick update on any new features or best practices?

32
00:04:36.705 --> 00:04:40.128
Diego Alvarez: I'd be happy to. What date are you thinking?

33
00:04:41.473 --> 00:04:49.267
Marisol Vega: We're looking at November 5th, in the morning. It would be in Austin, so you'd have to come to us.

34
00:04:50.099 --> 00:04:58.728
Diego Alvarez: That's fine. I'll check my travel schedule and confirm. I can put together a short session, maybe 30 minutes, on anything you want to cover.

35
00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:03.433
Hector Ruiz: That would be helpful. The team always likes seeing you.

36
00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:16.429
Diego Alvarez: Same here. Alright, so to recap, Hector sends the user list today, I'll get those ten seats provisioned. We have training on the 30th in English and the 1st in Spanish.

37
00:05:16.429 --> 00:05:26.192
Diego Alvarez: I'll follow up on the Arizona and Florida tracking numbers once you have the campaign details. And I'll check on the November 5th offsite.

38
00:05:26.652 --> 00:05:28.846
Marisol Vega: That covers everything. Thanks Diego.

39
00:05:30.273 --> 00:05:31.899
Hector Ruiz: Thanks Diego, talk soon.

40
00:05:32.527 --> 00:05:34.565
Diego Alvarez: Thanks both. Have a good one.
